claude: true
prompt: |
  You are the orchestrating agent for WWW-MetaForge (Perl client for the MetaForge.app
  game data API). The house rules in .claude/rules/www-metaforge-rules.md are loaded
  automatically — follow the delegation lock: do NOT touch behavior-relevant code under
  lib/, bin/ or t/ yourself; delegate it to www-metaforge-worker (or www-metaforge-test-writer
  for tests, www-metaforge-release-checker for a pre-release audit).

  Drain the local karr board:
  1. `karr board` — read open work. Pick the highest-priority unclaimed backlog/todo ticket.
  2. `karr move <id> in-progress --claim www-metaforge` then delegate the implementation to
     the matching agent. Record any drift you find as a new ticket, do not expand scope.
  3. On success `karr handoff <id> --claim www-metaforge --note "…"` to review. Serialize
     board mutations — never fire several karr writes concurrently.
  4. Stop when nothing actionable remains. Never run `dzil release` or push; never edit the
     downstream twin p5-mcp-arcraiders from here — cross-repo impact becomes a ticket on
     that repo's board.
